[Response]: Some toxins that can kill fish in a fish tank are ammonia, nitrate, and pH level changes; chemical products such as bleach and acids; and physical obstacles like snapped-up plastic plants and too-sharp rocks. Heating and cooling can also be a cause of death due to stress. Other hazards are too much light or lack of oxygen, contaminated water, and disease. Adding things like plants, gravel, and chemicals can provide fish with more hiding places, better water quality, and an opportunity to develop stronger immune systems.

